---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { proseClass } from './_seo';
---
<Base pageType="policy" title="Terms of use | SizeTune" description="Plain-language terms for using SizeTune: a free service provided as is. Check every result against your own form's requirements before you upload it." path="/terms/">
  <h1 class="mb-3 text-3xl font-bold">Terms of use</h1>
  <div class={proseClass}>
    <p>Last updated 12 November 2026. [[HUMAN: legal review pending. Have a lawyer review these terms before launch, then replace this marker with the review date or remove it.]]</p>

    <h2>Using the service</h2>
    <p>
      SizeTune is a free tool for reducing the file size of images. By using the site you agree to these terms. If you
      do not agree, please do not use it. You do not need an account, and we do not ask you for payment.
    </p>

    <h2>Provided as is</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided as is and as available. It may contain mistakes, may stop working, and may behave
      differently in different browsers and devices. Check your result against your form's requirements before you
      upload it. We cannot promise that a file will meet any requirement or be accepted by any organisation, and the
      guidance on this site is general information, not advice about any particular application.
    </p>

    <h2>Your images</h2>
    <p>
      You keep all rights in the images you use. Images are processed in your browser and the code of this site does
      not upload them, as described on the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>. You are responsible for having the
      right to use and change the images you choose, and for how you use the files you download.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not use the site in a way that breaks the law, interferes with how it works, or tries to harm others. Do not
      use the tool to change documents or pictures so as to mislead an organisation about who you are or what a
      document says.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, SizeTune and its owner are not responsible for losses that arise from using the
      site, including a rejected application, a missed deadline or a lost file. Nothing in these terms limits any
      right you have that cannot lawfully be limited.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes, law and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We may change the service or these terms, and the date at the top shows the latest version. These terms are
      governed by [[HUMAN: governing law and jurisdiction line, for example the country or state whose law applies and where disputes are heard]].
      Questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@sizetune.com">hello@sizetune.com</a>. See also the <a href="/about/">about page</a> for who runs the site.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
